# Freeze the character tools/keys/xsummon-priest.keys builds, so every check
# that runs that script can load him instead of rolling him again.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/xsummon-priest-save.keys 5
#
# THE CHARGEN BELOW IS A COPY of tools/keys/xsummon-priest.keys lines 1-56,
# deliberately unchanged, and the original is NOT edited. Copying rather than
# refactoring means no existing check changes what it measures; the same choice
# and the same warning are in tools/keys/lizardfolk-monk-save.keys.
#
# THE CUT IS AT LINE 56 AND NOT AT THE LAST "ENTER y", which is where the
# other copies in this directory end. A PRIEST'S CHARGEN RUNS PAST THE SKILL
# MANAGER: he picks a personality archetype and then four starting spells.
# Measured 2026-09-17 by cutting at line 53 instead -- the session stopped at
# "Learn which spell (1 left)?" and spent all 200 of @until's ESC passes there,
# because that screen is a menu wanting a letter. The four picks are the
# script's own generic "a a a a"; the spell this check actually needs, Holy
# Summoning I, it grants itself later through wizard mode, so nothing the check
# measures is decided here.
#
# WHY A CHARACTER IS FROZEN AT ALL: see tools/keys/chargen-default-save.keys.
# bd inc-vrt8.

# Prove that a priest cannot stack summons from one summoning spell.
#
# THE DEFECT (bd inc-j6ni). The engine carries its own one-at-a-time summon
# limiter: Magic::Summon aborts a cast when the caster still holds a live
# creature summoned by the SAME effect, but only for an effect flagged
# EF_XSUMMON (src/Effects.cpp:1383-1391). The wizard summoning line sets that
# flag. Holy Summoning I through VI and Summon Nature's Ally I through VI set
# no Flags clause at all, so a priest or druid could recast without limit --
# which is what Brian met in play on 2026-08-22, from a monster priest sitting
# behind Sanctuary.
#
# THE ORACLE is the spell's own refusal message, "The outsider you called
# before still serves you.", thrown as MSG_XSUMMON by the abort path and by
# nothing else. It appears on the SECOND cast and not on the first. On a module
# compiled from the pre-fix lib/pspells.irh the second cast summons a second
# outsider and says nothing.
#
# WHY WIZARD MODE. Two switches, and each removes a reason the run could fail
# for something other than the thing measured:
#   * Learn Any Spell puts Holy Summoning I in the book whatever god the seed
#     gave this priest, and whatever four spells generation offered.
#   * Infinite Mana keeps the second cast from being refused for 3 mana
#     (src/Magic.cpp:2658) before it ever reaches the summon guard.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
i       # Race:     [i] Orc
a       # Subrace:  [a] Orc (Standard)
g       # Class:    [g] Priest
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# The Skill Manager, three times -- once for the class pool, once for the pool
# that follows the choice of god, and once more. The conditionals are copied
# from chargen-priest.keys, where the reasons are written out: the domain
# prompt and the size of the rank pool both vary with the god.
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

a a
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

a       # Personality archetype
a a a a # Four starting spells

@dump:arrival

# HOW MANY KEYS THE OPENING WANTS IS A PROPERTY OF THE CHARACTER, so no fixed
# count is right for every chargen. Measured 2026-09-17: tools/keys/chargen.keys
# leaves NOTHING pending and reaches the System Menu on the first ESC, while
# tools/keys/chargen-rogue.keys leaves a god's speech and an AutoHide line, so
# the first ESC only dismisses a message. A hard-coded ESC ENTER SPACE, copied
# from tools/keys/lizardfolk-monk-save.keys, failed in both directions: it
# walked INTO the menu for the barbarian and fell short of it for the rogue.
# @until sends ESC as many times as this character needs and stops the moment
# the menu is up (src/Wposix.cpp:1318-1326).
# CHARGEN IS NOT OVER UNTIL THE ARCHETYPE IS PICKED, and ESC will not dismiss
# that screen -- it is a menu wanting a letter. Measured 2026-09-17: five of
# these save scripts reached "Your personality archetype has little direct
# influence..." and spent all 200 of @until's passes pressing ESC at it
# (src/Wposix.cpp:1568-1571). [a] is The Ambitious Conqueror; the choice only
# has to be the SAME one every time, because a fixture is a frozen character
# and the archetype is, in the game's own words, "largely a 'colour' choice".
@while "personality archetype" a

@until "System Menu" ESC

# @until only warns when it gives up (src/Wposix.cpp:1568-1571), so the
# assertion stays: it stops the run at exit 6 rather than pressing a letter
# into whatever screen is really there. [a] beside [b] is Save and Quit.
@expect "System Menu"
b                       # [b] Save and Continue (src/Player.cpp:843)

# The save is not written by the keypress. Case 2 of the System Menu sets the
# autosave flag and Timeout = 1 (src/Player.cpp:851-853); Game::Play writes the
# file at the top of the next pass of its loop (src/Main.cpp:266-275). This
# dump therefore fires AFTER the file is on disk, and photographs the engine's
# own "Autosave... done." line saying so.
@dump:saved

# NO @quit HERE, DELIBERATELY. @quit becomes KY_CMD_QUICK_QUIT
# (src/Wposix.cpp:1657-1664), which is Save and Quit: it would write the save a
# SECOND time and shuffle the first copy off to <name>.sav.backup, leaving the
# fixture a file no line of this script asked for. Letting the key script run
# out instead ends the session with exactly one save.
